    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50159" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰή</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῐ]</span>, exclam. of joy or
		enthusiasm, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰή, ἰή, ἰή</span>, <i><span class="en">
			Ar.
			<u>Pax</u>
			195
		</span></i>; esp. used in the cult of Apollo, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰὴ
			παιών</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
			453
		</span></i>, al.; <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰὴ παιῆον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Ap.</u>
					21
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				103
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Hec.</u>
				1.1.10
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλαλαὶ ἰὴ παιήων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Lys.</u>
					1291
				</span></i>
			; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰέ</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of grief, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				1004
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Supp.</u>
				114
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ag.</u>
				1485
			</span></i> (all lyr.). (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵη</span>
			v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Ap.</u>
			</span></i>ll.cc., where it is associated with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵει</span>, imper. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵημι</span>.)</div>
